  "constants": {"PCM_STALE_AFTER":45000},
  "note": "D52.4/D52.5 app-side audio transport watchdog (SPEC.md \"Audio transport liveness\"). Monotonic milliseconds. frames lists what arrives in order: track/audio/sources/trackEnd/stop on the recording's audio transport (id names the span), control is any frame on the control connection (ping/pong, meetings, status, result, hello). All spans are remote browser spans. Every audio-transport frame counts; control frames do not. The watchdog is armed only while an open span (track, not yet trackEnd or stop) has delivered audio. closeAtMs is when the app closes the transport (now - lastFrame >= PCM_STALE_AFTER while armed), or null if it never does (a frame arriving exactly at the deadline is too late); probes give closed-by-then at exact times, including the 1 ms before the boundary. The app closes through its EOF path (system/lost fallback). documentChanged (D57) is a control frame carrying the recording tab's pageState and documentGeneration, either optional, as a status reports them: navigating retires every open span and opens a departing window in which declared spans are retired; the window closes on the next present or on a new documentGeneration, never on the same one; a new documentGeneration retires the spans declared up to the last frame that still reported the old one, and a span declared after that stays armed. A track frame may carry documentGeneration (D61, extension 0.2.12): the app keeps the set of departed generations (navigating adds the current one and the generation of every open span; a change from a known generation adds the old one and the generation of every open span other than the new one), a span with a generation is dormant exactly when its generation is in that set, and the declaration-order rules apply only to spans without one; a generation that is not 1 to 200 UTF-8 bytes counts as absent, and none ever leaves the set. Track ids are unique for the session: a track frame for an id already declared on the transport, open or ended, changes no span (it keeps its first generation), though it is activity, whatever the host replies (an identical repeat of an open id is idempotent, a repeat of an ended id is refused).",
